Package: homelab-webtheme
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${perl:Depends}, perl (>= 5.36), libmojolicious-perl
Description: Shared header, footer and theme for the homelab web apps
 Gives every homelab Mojolicious app the same chrome -- the Silver Linings
 logo top-left opening an account dropdown, a shared footer, and one
 stylesheet -- so the apps read as one product rather than several that
 happen to share a domain, and so a new app inherits the look instead of
 re-deciding it.
 .
 Adopting it is one line: load the Homelab::WebTheme plugin, then include the
 homelab/head, homelab/header and homelab/footer partials from a layout.
 .
 The stylesheet is NOT shipped here. It is served from
 static.mailmasker.org/theme/v1/, so a visual change restyles every app with
 no rebuild and no redeploy. Only the markup ships in this package, because
 the header is server-rendered (it shows the signed-in address, and rendering
 it client-side would mean an API round trip and a flash of missing header).
 Styling is therefore instant; changing the header's STRUCTURE needs a package
 bump. That split is deliberate.
